# Data Science 3010: Coursework Repository

Welcome to the official repository for **Data Science 3010**. This repository contains all homework assignments, lab materials, and supporting datasets for the semester.

---

## 📂 Repository Structure

The repository is organized into the following directories:

```text
DS-3010/
├── data/                  # Shared datasets used across multiple assignments
├── homeworks/             # Individual homework folders (HW1, HW2, etc.)
│   ├── hw1/
│   ├── hw2/
│   └── ...
├── labs/                  # In-class lab exercises and notebooks
├── notebooks/             # Scratchpads and exploratory code examples
└── README.md              # Course overview and instructions (this file)
```

---

## 📝 Homework Structure

Each homework assignment within the `homeworks/` directory follows a standardized layout to ensure smooth grading and reproducibility:

```text
homeworks/hwX/
├── data/                  # Assignment-specific datasets (if applicable)
├── notebooks/             # Jupyter Notebooks containing your analysis
├── scripts/               # Python or R scripts (.py, .R) for modular code
├── outputs/               # Generated figures, tables, or exported CSVs
└── README.md              # Assignment-specific instructions and questions
```

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

1. **Clone the Repository:**
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/ds-3010-coursework.git
   cd ds-3010-coursework
   ```

2. **Set Up Your Environment:**
   Make sure you have your virtual environment activated and dependencies installed (refer to the course requirements file for specific library versions).

3. **Submitting Homework:**
   * Place your completed work inside the respective `homeworks/hwX/` folder.
   * Ensure all notebooks run cleanly from top to bottom before committing.
   * Push your changes to your remote fork or submit according to instructor guidelines.

---

*Happy coding and exploring data!*
